From b6c5e8bb6fd627d27eb7013d2d04470c97f672ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for yrn-mwathi)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] End the demo: delete demo sign-ins, campaigns and data in one
 step; it stays ended
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Settings → Campaigns gets a "Demo aspirants" box: lists the demo sign-ins and
  campaigns, "End demo and delete demo data" (type END DEMO), and "Start demo
  again" once ended (needs DEMO_ASPIRANTS_PASSWORD).
- POST /api/tenancy/demo/end (admin): in one transaction deletes the demo
  campaigns and every record they own, the demo sign-ins (only accounts the
  demo created), their 2FA records and open sessions, and the demo group; then
  records demo.aspirants.ended so a restart doesn't re-create the demo even if
  DEMO_ASPIRANTS_PASSWORD is still set. GET /tenancy/demo, POST /tenancy/demo/start.
- Campaign deletion moved to lib/campaign-delete.ts and shared by "Delete
  permanently" and "End demo" (children before parents, never the primary).

Verified: 81/81 acceptance tests, typecheck + production build, and an end-to-
end run with row-level security on shared tables: end demo removed 3 sign-ins,
3 campaigns and 588 records with nothing left; the open demo session was signed
out; a restart did not re-create it; "Start demo again" restored it; ordinary
delete still works; candidate role gets 403.
